		<section label="Stuck" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing id="variations-stuck">
			<example "Stuck" description="A table can scroll horizontally, with its head, foot, first or last column staying stuck (`stuck`).  You can freely stick any combination like `stuck=\"head first\"`, `\"foot first last\"`, `\"head foot first\"`, `\"first last\"`, etc.">
				<message slot="description" state="info" size="small">A stuck table possibly needs to be wrapped into an overflowing container like a <link link="/components/ui/ui-container.html">scrolling container</link> or <link link="/components/ui/ui-segment.html">scrolling segment</link>. If you don't want an extra wrapper, use <text code>overflowing</text> on the table; this only works if the table's columns exceed the available width.</message>
